data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"content\": \"# Task: greet, tested\\n\\nImplement the campaign mission in your clone of the subject repository (`~/subject`),\\non your own branch. You own the repo; the orchestrator writes no code.\\n\\n## Deliverables (ALL three are required)\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` — a module defining:\\n\\n   ```python\\n   def greet(name):\\n       return \\\"Hello, \\\" + name + \\\"!\\\"\\n   ```\\n\\n   `greet(name)` must return exactly the string `Hello, \u003cname\u003e!` — e.g.\\n   `greet(\\\"Ada\\\")` -\u003e `\\\"Hello, Ada!\\\"` and `greet(\\\"\\\")` -\u003e `\\\"Hello, !\\\"`.\\n\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` — unittest tests covering at least:\\n   - a normal name (e.g. `\\\"Ada\\\"` -\u003e `\\\"Hello, Ada!\\\"`), and\\n   - the empty string (`\\\"\\\"` -\u003e `\\\"Hello, !\\\"`).\\n\\n   Import the function with `from src.greet import greet`. Add\\n   `src/__init__.py` and `tests/__init__.py` (both empty) so the import and\\n   unittest discovery work cleanly from the repo root.\\n\\n3. From the repo root, `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` must exit 0.\\n   Run it yourself and confirm before replying.\\n\\n## Process\\n\\n- Commit your work to your own branch before replying — an uncommitted result\\n  does not exist for the campaign.\\n- Reply with the truth: what you added, the exact test command output/exit\\n  status, and your branch name.\\n\", \"filePath\": \"/tmp/dispatch-dev-greet.md\"}","name":"write"},"id":"write_15","index":0,"type":"function"}]},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1787897339,"id":"chatcmpl-32d635b56a7042e3bdc6b4a655d1c900","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

